					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "BAG\n\nBag is a node that can be best described by visual storytelling. \nImagine you have a bag in which you put a set of integers. \nNow pull those numbers out one at a time at random. \nWhen you’re done, put all the numbers back and start over. \nNow you know how the Bag node works!\n\nUse the min and max values to set up the range of values that are in the bag. \nSend a trigger to have the bag output a value.\n You can also use a trigger to reset the bag, putting all the values back in.\n\nThe No Duplicates attribute makes sure that the first pull from the bag is not the same as the last pull (before the reset)."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 275.8914794921875,
					"width": 832.15374755859375,
					"x": 7.27375411987304688,
					"y": -945.3878173828125
				},
